WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.207
We just discussed and saw that routing can be enabled in Windows Server. Now, let's see how this is set up and configured.

00:07.207 --> 00:19.827
To install this role, I'll click, from Server Manager, Add roles and features, I'll keep clicking Next until I get to the Server Roles area, and I'll select Remote Access.

00:19.827 --> 00:34.773
Then I'll click next a couple of times, I'll get to Role Services, and I'm going to click DirectAccess and VPN and add the features necessary, and then the same for Routing.

00:34.773 --> 00:45.168
I'll click Next and then I'll click Install.  Now, while this is installing, let me show you another server where this stuff has already been installed.

00:45.168 --> 01:02.069
I've opened in this server, from Server Manager and Tools, Remote Access Management, and I've selected DirectAccess and VPN.

01:02.069 --> 01:10.879
Now from here I'm going to click Open RRAS management. This is going to open a separate window, which I'm going to maximize.

01:10.879 --> 01:23.083
This has not yet been configured, so I will right-click this server, and I'll click Configure and Enable Routing and Remote Access. Start the Wizard.

01:23.083 --> 01:30.637
I'll click Custom configuration, and from here I'm going to set up NAT and LAN routing.

01:30.637 --> 01:38.220
I'll click Next, double-check and make sure this is what we want here, and then click Finish.

